      ],
      "extract": "The correlations of Dirac operator eigenvalues in QCD and related theories have been shown to have a fascinating relation to Random Matrix Theory. There are two very different domains of interest here. One is the so-called ``bulk'' of the eigenvalue spectrum of the Dirac operator, far from both the infrared and the ultraviolet ends. The other is the so-called ``hard edge'' at $\\lambda \\sim 0, ~i.e.$ the infrared end",
      "extractCut": true
