      "extract": "\\label{quenched} For our quenched finite temperature Monte Carlo simulations we have used lattices with temporal extent $N_t=4$ and up to three spatial volumes: $8^3$, $12^3$ and $16^3$. For $N_t=4$ the deconfinement phase transition for SU(3) pure gauge theory with Wilson action has been very accurately determined, occurring at lattice gauge coupling $\\beta_c=5.6925(2)$~\\cite{T_c}. It has for long been assumed that",
